  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nAside from an isolated lake enhanced shower or two early this\nmorning, mainly dry conditions expected today through Sunday as\nhigh pressure builds across the region. Warming temperatures\nexpected through the weekend although moisture return will be a\nbit delayed, with humidity ramping up by early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nModels have trended towards a less amplified ridge across the\nGreat Lakes Sunday night, with the potential for upstream\nconvection/MCS activity through the Great Lakes impacting far\nnortheast Ohio and northwest PA. The ridge may amplify a bit\nMonday into Tuesday over the area providing dry conditions,\nhowever an active zonal flow regime through the Great Lakes may\nend up shifting a bit further south impacting the local area.\nHigher confidence in shower/thunderstorm chances by mid to late\nweek across the area as a cold front settles south into the area\nand the mid/upper flow becomes northwest.",
